From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship toml++'s and pybind11's licences in the wheel's dist-info

The pytomlpp._impl extension compiles in the header-only toml++
library from the third_party/tomlplusplus git submodule (marzer/
tomlplusplus at c635f218c0aefc801d9748841930365e54fe3089, MIT) and the
pybind11 headers that setup_requires pulls in (pybind11~=2.8, i.e.
2.13.6, BSD-3-Clause). Both licences require their copyright notice to
accompany binary redistributions.

setup.cfg sets the deprecated singular `license_file = LICENSE`, which
turns off setuptools' default LICEN[CS]E* root glob, so only pytomlpp's
own LICENSE reaches dist-info/licenses/. Reproduced against the real
pytomlpp-1.0.13-cp311-cp311-musllinux_1_1_x86_64.whl from PyPI: its
dist-info carries only LICENSE.

Add both texts unchanged at the project root (toml++'s from the
submodule commit above, pybind11's from the 2.13.6 release) as
LICENSE.tomlplusplus and LICENSE.pybind11, and list them with
pytomlpp's own LICENSE under `license_files`.

third_party/optional.hpp is CC0-1.0 and carries no notice requirement.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this port may only touch riseproject-dev/python-wheels]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 LICENSE.pybind11     | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.tomlplusplus | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 setup.cfg            |  5 ++++-
 3 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.pybind11
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.tomlplusplus

diff --git a/LICENSE.pybind11 b/LICENSE.pybind11
